WEBVTT

00:04.850 --> 00:13.110
<b>A Playthrough of a Certain DUDE's
VRMMO LIFE</b>

01:30.480 --> 01:34.490
<b>Episode 11</b>

01:30.480 --> 01:34.490
<b>Earth Finds a Baby Dragon</b>

01:41.110 --> 01:42.260
A dragon?

01:46.660 --> 01:48.430
They all disappeared...

01:48.430 --> 01:50.630
They were NPCs?

01:55.220 --> 01:59.770
It wouldn't be right to 
just abandon it, would it?

02:00.940 --> 02:02.800
Whew!

02:05.310 --> 02:06.870
What?

02:06.870 --> 02:08.290
Um...

02:08.290 --> 02:10.060
Food, maybe?

02:13.110 --> 02:14.590
I guess this'll work.

02:21.810 --> 02:25.690
Well, I saved this dragon, 
but now what do I do with her?

02:28.320 --> 02:30.880
I could go back to First, but...

02:36.010 --> 02:38.230
No way. I'd stand out too much.

02:38.230 --> 02:40.530
Maybe the Fairy Kingdom, then?

02:41.090 --> 02:45.730
But there's a chance that 
bringing this dragon there

02:45.730 --> 02:48.280
will cause some kind of huge problem...

02:52.270 --> 02:56.130
I guess the first thing I need to 
do is find some more food for her.

02:56.490 --> 03:00.490
I did come out here to test 
my new bow, after all.

03:10.610 --> 03:14.810
<i>Every living thing looks cute 
when it's a baby, I guess.</i>

03:23.050 --> 03:24.110
What?

03:24.110 --> 03:25.780
You want this, too?

03:26.690 --> 03:28.370
Okay, fine.

03:28.370 --> 03:29.770
Give me a sec.

03:37.770 --> 03:39.520
<i>I can't believe it...</i>

03:44.030 --> 03:46.370
<i>She ate so much food!</i>

03:49.890 --> 03:51.510
They say journeys are more fun with friends,

03:51.510 --> 03:53.380
and you should try to help 
people you meet, but...

03:53.630 --> 03:57.080
I wonder if that goes for dragons, too.

03:57.640 --> 03:59.540
All right...

03:59.540 --> 04:01.870
Queen, can you drop by for a second?

04:02.590 --> 04:03.530
Hello!

04:03.530 --> 04:04.670
I'm here, just like you asked!

04:04.870 --> 04:08.340
It's me, your lover, Queenie!

04:08.140 --> 04:09.310
<b>Grr</b>

04:09.310 --> 04:11.000
Sorry, Queen.

04:11.000 --> 04:12.620
We've got a problem.

04:12.620 --> 04:14.110
A problem?

04:15.700 --> 04:18.510
What's a baby red dragon doing here?

04:18.510 --> 04:20.700
So I was right. It's a big deal.

04:21.350 --> 04:22.720
So this is what happened...

04:23.660 --> 04:25.670
I understand what happened.

04:25.670 --> 04:28.300
But this is definitely a big problem.

04:28.300 --> 04:29.280
It's that big a deal?

04:29.990 --> 04:33.000
Wild dragons never leave the
 borders of their kingdom,

04:33.000 --> 04:37.870
so that their terrible power 
doesn't cause needless conflict.

04:37.870 --> 04:39.390
Wild dragons?

04:39.390 --> 04:41.140
Are they different than regular dragons?

04:41.140 --> 04:42.090
Yes.

04:42.510 --> 04:46.020
They're both extremely powerful, but...

04:46.620 --> 04:49.930
The dragons have learned 
to control their power

04:49.930 --> 04:53.130
and are starting to learn to get 
along with the other races.

04:53.520 --> 04:57.400
But wild dragons have given up
 on controlling their power,

04:57.400 --> 04:59.690
and isolated themselves instead.

04:59.690 --> 05:02.380
Given up on controlling their power?

05:02.380 --> 05:06.420
And to make matters worse, 
that's a red dragon.

05:06.420 --> 05:07.540
What do you mean?

05:07.830 --> 05:11.260
Red dragons are much 
stronger than the others.

05:11.260 --> 05:13.970
They're a symbol of their nation.

05:13.970 --> 05:15.950
The royal family of the Wild Dragon Kingdom.

05:16.640 --> 05:18.860
And their child was kidnapped?

05:18.860 --> 05:21.290
Yes, this is a huge problem.

05:21.290 --> 05:24.790
If they find out, there's no telling 
what they might do in their anger.

05:26.570 --> 05:28.460
Trouble, Your Highness.

05:28.730 --> 05:32.270
There are red dragons 
heading here at top speed.

05:32.590 --> 05:35.060
You need to return to the castle...

05:39.900 --> 05:43.860
Y-You stupid queen! What are you doing?!

05:43.860 --> 05:47.130
Why would you kidnap a red dragon baby?!

05:47.130 --> 05:48.930
Wh-What do you mean, stupid?

05:48.930 --> 05:51.210
Even I wouldn't do something like that!

05:51.210 --> 05:53.700
So what's it doing here, then?

05:53.700 --> 05:55.690
It was Earth who...

05:56.370 --> 05:59.710
So what direction are the 
dragons coming from?

06:09.150 --> 06:10.370
There they are.

06:20.100 --> 06:20.900
<i>They're huge!</i>

06:21.320 --> 06:24.050
<i>If one of these went on a rampage, 
it would be a disaster!</i>

06:24.630 --> 06:28.410
Was it you who kidnapped our child?!

06:29.240 --> 06:31.060
I can hear his voice directly in my head...

06:31.540 --> 06:33.030
Wait!

06:33.030 --> 06:33.890
This man—

06:33.890 --> 06:36.420
Silence, Fairy Queen!

06:36.740 --> 06:40.560
We're talking to him right now.

06:43.100 --> 06:45.640
Child of man, answer us.

06:45.640 --> 06:48.090
Why did you kidnap our child?

06:48.560 --> 06:50.420
I don't know why your child was kidnapped.

06:50.820 --> 06:54.040
The ones who did it are probably dead.

06:54.040 --> 06:57.350
I simply found him and took care him.

06:57.350 --> 07:01.760
And you expect us to believe that?

07:02.210 --> 07:04.660
I understand that you doubt me.

07:04.660 --> 07:07.020
But I'm telling the truth!

07:11.780 --> 07:13.320
Very well.

07:13.320 --> 07:17.130
Then bring me our child.

07:19.300 --> 07:26.080
Do that and I will believe you, 
out of respect for your courage.

07:26.620 --> 07:28.040
Earth...

07:28.040 --> 07:29.120
It's fine.

07:29.930 --> 07:31.380
It's just fine.

07:53.920 --> 07:56.360
Oh, my child!

07:59.160 --> 08:02.290
My apologies, child of man.

08:02.560 --> 08:05.590
We have just seen our child's memories.

08:05.590 --> 08:09.520
What you said is indeed true.

08:10.620 --> 08:13.600
You fed her, too, I see.

08:13.600 --> 08:14.550
You have my gratitude.

08:14.990 --> 08:19.540
I also want to apologize for 
needlessly suspecting you.

08:19.540 --> 08:21.730
Ask for anything you want.

08:21.730 --> 08:23.380
All right, I will.

08:23.860 --> 08:28.360
Please don't hold the Fairy Kingdom 
responsible for what happened today.

08:28.980 --> 08:33.190
And pretend that we have never met.

08:33.730 --> 08:36.420
I understand why you'd want 
to protect the fairies.

08:36.420 --> 08:39.440
But why pretend we never met?

08:39.810 --> 08:43.870
I prefer peace and quiet. 
I don't want to attract attention.

08:43.870 --> 08:48.460
It's not that you don't want to 
be associated with us, correct?

08:48.460 --> 08:49.540
Very well, then.

08:49.830 --> 08:54.120
Yes. We shall grant your wish.

08:56.760 --> 09:00.080
We shall return to our lands, then.

09:00.080 --> 09:02.580
Farewell, child of man.

09:21.860 --> 09:23.640
It worked, huh?

09:23.640 --> 09:25.820
Yeah. We got lucky.

09:25.820 --> 09:30.510
Thank you for thinking about 
the Fairy Kingdom, too.

09:30.510 --> 09:32.670
As Queen, you have my gratitude.

09:32.670 --> 09:35.100
<i>As Queen, huh?</i>

09:35.100 --> 09:37.230
<i>She's growing up.</i>

09:37.610 --> 09:40.190
What will you be doing now?

09:40.190 --> 09:45.130
If you don't have any plans, why not 
come to the castle so I can thank you?

09:46.050 --> 09:48.730
I'd rather go to a town than the castle.

09:48.730 --> 09:51.470
I'd like to get some work.

09:51.470 --> 09:53.160
I see.

09:53.160 --> 09:55.910
I'll see you're given a ride, then.

09:55.910 --> 09:56.820
Pikasha!

10:00.720 --> 10:03.130
Thank you. And if you could—

10:03.130 --> 10:04.070
Of course.

10:04.350 --> 10:08.640
I will see to it that no one knows that
you were involved with this.

10:08.640 --> 10:09.860
Thanks.

10:09.860 --> 10:12.510
I don't want to attract any more 
attention than I already have.

10:14.030 --> 10:15.880
All right, I'm counting on you!

10:15.880 --> 10:17.940
Yes, leave it to me!

10:19.180 --> 10:21.600
<b>Fairy Kingdom East Fort Town</b>

10:20.630 --> 10:21.460
Huh?

10:21.930 --> 10:24.140
<b>Sunflower Tavern</b>

10:22.670 --> 10:24.150
You're kidding me...

10:25.690 --> 10:28.560
There's barely any work.

10:28.560 --> 10:32.100
Oh, it's your first time here, huh?

10:32.360 --> 10:36.780
Um, is there just no demand 
for adventurers here?

10:36.780 --> 10:38.690
No, that's not true.

10:38.690 --> 10:41.020
There were a lot of jobs at first.

10:41.280 --> 10:45.320
But human adventurers took them all.

10:45.640 --> 10:48.890
All the inns are like this now.

10:48.890 --> 10:51.130
I see.

10:51.130 --> 10:52.770
Oh, dear.

10:53.250 --> 10:55.300
If you want work that bad,

10:55.300 --> 10:59.380
why not work here while you stay the night?

11:01.280 --> 11:03.500
Table 7's food is ready.

11:04.190 --> 11:05.480
Okay!

11:09.370 --> 11:11.290
Let me read your order back to you.

11:11.290 --> 11:12.150
First...

11:12.700 --> 11:15.470
Hey, I don't have my food yet!

11:15.470 --> 11:17.020
Sorry!

11:21.150 --> 11:23.360
Why am I doing the cooking, too?

11:23.360 --> 11:25.030
Here's the next order.

11:25.030 --> 11:25.960
Okay!

11:25.960 --> 11:29.510
<i>It's just like being a 
part-timer at a restaurant!</i>

11:30.830 --> 11:32.660
It's finally over..

11:32.660 --> 11:35.150
Good work today!

11:35.590 --> 11:39.200
You were a huge help.

11:39.500 --> 11:41.140
Here's your pay!

11:41.140 --> 11:43.150
Thanks.

11:44.410 --> 11:47.000
I'll be going to bed.

11:47.000 --> 11:49.690
Thanks. Sweet dreams!

11:53.720 --> 11:56.870
I started the day by finding a dragon baby,

11:56.870 --> 11:59.650
and ended it as a part-timer 
at a restaurant...

11:59.650 --> 12:02.140
<i>One More</i>'s really got everything...

12:07.580 --> 12:10.930
But well, it's kind of fun.

12:10.930 --> 12:14.250
I could make some money and 
open my own restaurant.

12:14.250 --> 12:15.990
That might be one way to play...

12:15.990 --> 12:21.580
You know, I think this game 
has too many things to do.

12:23.210 --> 12:29.380
So we all agree to continue 
running <i>One More</i>, then.

12:30.640 --> 12:33.820
Good, good. These results are spectacular.

12:34.060 --> 12:36.460
That's all well and good, old man.

12:36.460 --> 12:39.410
But how are things looking 
with the two of them?

12:39.750 --> 12:41.160
You'll be shocked.

12:41.160 --> 12:45.500
Involvement with one of the players 
has caused EA to learn to laugh,

12:45.500 --> 12:47.830
and EB to learn to be angry.

12:49.010 --> 12:52.330
I was surprised when I first saw it, as well.

12:52.700 --> 12:55.990
EA had become almost completely emotionless,

12:55.990 --> 13:00.820
and EB reacted by constantly 
acting like a spoiled child...

13:01.230 --> 13:04.250
I can't believe the two of them 
have changed so much.

13:04.250 --> 13:05.990
Unbelievable.

13:05.990 --> 13:09.320
I'd been so focused on showing 
that world to my daughter...

13:09.320 --> 13:11.540
I didn't realize there was 
someone like that out there.

13:12.440 --> 13:14.460
He's an interesting man.

13:14.460 --> 13:16.730
What, you know him?

13:16.730 --> 13:20.090
Yes. I'm a player, too.

13:20.660 --> 13:25.120
Yes, I'm very curious about this player.

13:25.120 --> 13:30.480
But that's all the more reason to
 continue operating the game.

13:32.450 --> 13:37.030
Yes. We need <i>One More</i> to 
train our AIs, as well!

13:41.460 --> 13:43.380
<b>"A Challenge from the Departed" PvP Tournament Winner!

The Challenge from the Departed PvP tournament
was recently held between 20 Liberators in the town of Nexia.
The winner was a five-man party led by Silver.
They defeated Glad's party, the pre-tournament favorite,
as well as Ayame's archer party.
 Silver's party will be awarded 20 million gloh.</b>

13:43.380 --> 13:49.630
So Silver's party won the "Challenge 
from the Departed" PvP tournament, huh?

13:50.060 --> 13:53.790
I guess Glad gets to taste the 
agony of defeat this time.

13:56.830 --> 13:59.310
The wind feels so good...

13:59.830 --> 14:03.480
It's been a while since this 
game's been so relaxing for me.

14:05.460 --> 14:09.710
This is actually what I wanted 
when I started this game.

14:10.230 --> 14:14.490
But I've been attracting attention instead.

14:15.730 --> 14:18.620
I kind of wonder what I'm doing.

14:19.230 --> 14:25.540
Well, it was fun, though. 
Being able to run around and move like that...

14:27.220 --> 14:31.390
<i>When I was little, I used to run 
around and play all the time.</i>

14:31.720 --> 14:33.280
<i>But once I got older,</i>

14:33.280 --> 14:37.950
<i>I was so busy with work, I didn't get 
a lot of chances to exercise.</i>

14:38.470 --> 14:40.240
<i>And the next thing I knew,</i>

14:40.240 --> 14:43.740
<i>I was so out of shape that 
I was feeling depressed.</i>

14:44.920 --> 14:48.410
<i>So I decided that I could
 at least come here...</i>

14:49.000 --> 14:51.170
<i>And it's so much fun to be able to do things</i>

14:51.170 --> 14:55.230
<i>that I could never do in the real world, 
even when I was younger.</i>

14:58.870 --> 15:00.750
<i>So I let things get out of hand.</i>

15:01.430 --> 15:07.470
<i>'Cause in the real world, my body and my 
heart don't work like they did when I was little.</i>

15:09.660 --> 15:12.080
Wait, why am I crying?

15:13.670 --> 15:16.220
<i>It's not a good idea for me to be alone.</i>

15:16.560 --> 15:20.060
<i>I think about stuff I shouldn't 
and get depressed.</i>

15:21.330 --> 15:24.860
<i>I'm better off when there's 
crazy stuff going on around me.</i>

15:27.850 --> 15:32.040
<i>Fortunately, I know lots of crazy people.</i>

15:33.050 --> 15:38.730
<i>Actually, maybe that means 
I've been kind of harsh on them.</i>

15:38.730 --> 15:41.030
<i>I need to be nicer.</i>

15:42.080 --> 15:44.040
<b>Eastern City Sezanah</b>

15:44.510 --> 15:46.500
<i>Or so I thought, but...</i>

15:46.500 --> 15:49.600
This is way too sudden!

15:49.600 --> 15:50.890
What is?

15:52.840 --> 15:54.110
Nothing.

15:54.110 --> 15:55.480
Never mind.

15:55.480 --> 15:59.590
So, what's so urgent you needed to 
summon me here the second I arrived in town?

15:59.780 --> 16:03.510
I thought you might want to see me!

16:03.510 --> 16:04.540
Shaddup!

16:06.130 --> 16:09.020
And who might you be?

16:09.280 --> 16:13.750
I was hoping Her Majesty 
might introduce me, but...

16:15.370 --> 16:19.730
I'm a green dragon. We are wild dragons that 
have the power to control the wind.

16:19.730 --> 16:21.330
A wild dragon?

16:21.330 --> 16:26.080
I heard your race tries to avoid 
contact with the other races.

16:26.500 --> 16:29.640
We green dragons are an exception.

16:29.640 --> 16:34.270
We're less powerful than the other wild 
dragons, but far faster and more agile,

16:34.270 --> 16:36.260
and we can take human form, too.

16:36.610 --> 16:40.370
Thus, we sometimes serve as messengers.

16:40.370 --> 16:41.610
I see.

16:41.610 --> 16:43.780
I understand who you are.

16:43.780 --> 16:44.980
But...

16:45.240 --> 16:48.150
What would someone like that want with me?

16:48.150 --> 16:51.720
You really have no idea why I'm here?

16:51.720 --> 16:54.400
I'm not sure...

16:55.210 --> 16:59.000
All I can think of is that 
I returned the red dragon baby.

16:59.000 --> 17:01.650
But they agreed to pretend 
that never happened.

17:01.650 --> 17:02.780
Yes.

17:02.780 --> 17:06.460
There's actually a problem 
with the young lady.

17:06.770 --> 17:07.740
A problem?

17:07.740 --> 17:08.800
Yes.

17:08.800 --> 17:11.250
After returning to our kingdom...

17:14.930 --> 17:16.940
she's nearly stopped eating entirely.

17:17.850 --> 17:18.920
Huh?

17:19.320 --> 17:23.750
If she's going to grow up into a big, 
strong dragon, she needs to eat.

17:24.100 --> 17:26.370
But she...

17:27.540 --> 17:31.930
She only eats about half what 
a normal dragon her age eats!

17:33.980 --> 17:35.560
And not only that...

17:35.560 --> 17:38.640
Teach me how to become human!

17:39.330 --> 17:42.690
She came to us and asked that...

17:42.690 --> 17:46.510
And you've been told to find out why?

17:46.510 --> 17:50.260
Yes. Do you have any idea?

17:50.260 --> 17:52.280
No, not really.

17:52.720 --> 17:56.590
When I found her, she ate a whole lot.

17:56.590 --> 17:57.830
Really?

17:57.830 --> 17:58.900
Yes.

18:01.230 --> 18:02.240
Hey.

18:03.550 --> 18:07.100
Don't you suppose that 
your cooking was just too good?

18:14.390 --> 18:17.350
What did you feed her?

18:17.350 --> 18:21.150
Soup and Hamburg steak... a lot of both...

18:22.120 --> 18:24.460
Soup? Hamburg steak?

18:24.460 --> 18:26.280
What are those things?

18:26.280 --> 18:28.450
They're, um... well...

18:32.940 --> 18:34.240
<i>Did I screw up?</i>

18:36.880 --> 18:38.880
This is delicious!

18:39.640 --> 18:43.000
I can see why the young lady isn't 
interested in our food anymore!

18:43.000 --> 18:44.190
Right?

18:44.540 --> 18:47.640
His cooking is the best.

18:47.950 --> 18:49.290
Ahem.

18:50.240 --> 18:51.760
Sorry, can I have seconds?

18:51.760 --> 18:52.740
Me, too!

18:53.930 --> 18:55.600
You may not have seconds!

18:55.600 --> 18:57.620
What did you even come here for?

18:57.620 --> 19:01.030
And Queen! Don't expect 
me to cook for you, too!

19:01.650 --> 19:03.220
I-I'm sorry.

19:03.530 --> 19:05.210
I don't know what came over me.

19:05.620 --> 19:06.240
Um...

19:06.810 --> 19:11.130
Can you please make some more? 
I want to take it back for her.

19:11.130 --> 19:13.600
Look, I can't just...

19:13.600 --> 19:14.980
Please!

19:14.980 --> 19:19.000
If I go back without any,
 they'll be infuriated with me!

19:19.000 --> 19:21.510
But I don't have the ingredients!

19:21.760 --> 19:24.460
Then I shall procure them!

19:26.800 --> 19:28.700
Does he have to go that far?

19:32.350 --> 19:33.800
Thank you!

19:36.320 --> 19:38.040
I'll be going, then.

19:38.040 --> 19:40.900
Just you wait, young lady!

19:42.070 --> 19:47.650
Hey, didn't you say the wild dragons 
didn't interact with the other races?

19:47.650 --> 19:50.620
Yes, that's how it usually works.

19:50.620 --> 19:54.220
But you may have just changed that.

19:55.850 --> 19:57.930
I feel tired all of a sudden.

19:57.930 --> 19:59.330
I'm going back to the inn.

20:03.330 --> 20:06.000
You should come to the castle this time.

20:06.000 --> 20:08.940
I'll prepare the best room 
we have for you.

20:09.760 --> 20:12.690
And then you'll sneak 
into the bed, won't you?

20:12.690 --> 20:14.850
I can tell exactly what you're up to!

20:16.150 --> 20:17.120
Wait!

20:17.460 --> 20:18.480
Farewell!

20:18.480 --> 20:19.290
Jump!

20:19.660 --> 20:22.190
Wait, Earth!

20:23.060 --> 20:27.230
<i>I know I said I'd be nicer, 
but there are limits!</i>

20:27.630 --> 20:29.950
<i>Still, those wild dragons...</i>

20:29.950 --> 20:33.450
<i>Did I just open relations with an 
isolated race with my cooking?</i>

20:45.160 --> 20:47.460
Another plate!

20:47.460 --> 20:48.260
Understood.

20:49.240 --> 20:50.700
What's going on?

20:50.700 --> 20:52.300
What is this?

20:52.500 --> 20:55.600
This is cooking, Sire!

20:55.950 --> 20:57.030
Cooking!

20:57.030 --> 20:58.150
Indeed.

20:58.150 --> 21:01.690
A technology that makes 
food even more delicious.

21:02.120 --> 21:05.750
She simply missed the taste of this.

21:09.040 --> 21:10.470
Astonishing...

21:10.470 --> 21:14.610
I had no idea that
 child of man had such a skill.

21:21.210 --> 21:23.220
<b>Several Days Later</b>

21:22.430 --> 21:23.690
No luck, huh?

21:26.070 --> 21:28.300
<i>I've gotten to the point 
where it looks right,</i>

21:28.650 --> 21:32.200
but it tastes... terrible.

21:34.550 --> 21:36.590
I guess it's pointless to 
try and imitate its appearance

21:36.590 --> 21:39.140
without learning the basics of the art.

21:42.190 --> 21:46.550
Should I ask the king for 
permission to go learn from him?

21:47.600 --> 21:52.590
No, it wouldn't be appropriate 
